*   Task: Parallelize the N-body acceleration kernel using OpenMP.
    *   Kernel: A classic all-pairs calculation (O(n^2)).
    *   Input: `px`, `py`, `pz` (positions), `m` (masses).
    *   Output: `ax`, `ay`, `az` (accelerations).
    *   Constraint: Only modify code between `=== KERNEL BEGIN ===` and `=== KERNEL END ===`.
    *   Target: Apple M4 (10 cores: 4 P-cores, 6 E-cores).
    *   Compilation: `clang -O2 -fopenmp` (OpenMP 5.1).
    *   Performance goal: Maximize speed, handling heterogeneous cores.

    ```c
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        double sx = 0.0, sy = 0.0, sz = 0.0;
        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
            double dx = px[j] - px[i], dy = py[j] - py[i], dz = pz[j] - pz[i];
            double r2 = dx * dx + dy * dy + dz * dz + 1e-9;
            double inv = m[j] / (r2 * sqrt(r2));
            sx += dx * inv; sy += dy * inv; sz += dz * inv;
        }
        ax[i] = sx; ay[i] = sy; az[i] = sz;
    }
    ```
